# Chaos: the helper's item slots show the target cursor like "Use with"; right-click or Escape cancels (after 0001-0065).
# Owner: clicking a healing slot (spell, potion, mana training), a tool, timer, rune, equipment, supply, food or
# stamina slot did not change the cursor. The helper only called g_mouse.pushCursor('target'); with the system cursor
# (the client's default) that shows nothing. game_interface's startUseWith also calls g_mouse.setGrabber(widget,
# 'target'). Each of the nine pickers now calls ChaosItemPicker.begin(grabber) once its onMouseRelease is set and
# ChaosItemPicker.finish() where it popped the cursor (overlay game_helperrotation/itempicker.lua, tested); without
# that module the old calls run. A right-click or Escape runs the slot's handler off the window: nothing is picked.
